# tools/cr/crypto_mldsa_sample_witness.rish -- the ML-DSA sampling rung: FIPS 204's RejNTTPoly (Algorithm 30, the uniform public matrix A from a
# SHAKE128 stream), RejBoundedPoly (Algorithm 31, the small secret s1/s2 in [-eta, eta] from a SHAKE256 stream via CoefFromHalfByte), and
# SampleInBall (Algorithm 29, the sparse challenge c with exactly tau coefficients of +/-1), authored in pure Rye as Season G's third post-quantum
# SIGNATURE rung, standing on the GREEN base ring crypto/mldsa_ring.rye and the GREEN XOF crypto/shake.rye. The signature-side counterpart to
# crypto/mlkem_sample.rye, with one new shape the KEM never needs: the weight-tau ball.
#
# Season: crypto -- Season G's ML-DSA ladder, rung 3. Turns a seed into ring elements; it holds no key and runs no protocol.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260816/20260816-161537_post-quantum-mlkem-mldsa-pivot.md (the ML-DSA ladder). Rye-first spine:
# active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md.
# Clean-room: the FIPS 204 algorithms and constants (q = 8380417, eta 2/4, tau 39/49/60, CoefFromThreeBytes/CoefFromHalfByte) are the public NIST
# standard's own; the arithmetic is our own Rye, never a copied line (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# crypto/mldsa_sample.rye proves itself by SELF-CONSISTENCY with no external dependency -- the pattern crypto/mlkem_sample.rye stood on: RejNTTPoly
# matches a structurally independent 24-bit bit-reader over the same GREEN SHAKE128 stream byte-for-byte across 24 seeds (each draw canonical and
# spanning a wide slice of [0, q)); RejBoundedPoly carries the CoefFromHalfByte known-answers, the centered range [-eta, eta] at both eta, and
# determinism; and the decisive one, SampleInBall produces exactly tau nonzero coefficients each +/-1 (Hamming weight tau), deterministic, across
# all three tau. Purely local -- no key, no network, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_mldsa_sample_witness.rish

say "crypto-mldsa-sample: Language EN — the ML-DSA sampling rung: FIPS 204's RejNTTPoly (uniform public matrix A from SHAKE128), RejBoundedPoly (the small secret in [-eta, eta] from SHAKE256), and SampleInBall (the sparse challenge c of exactly tau +/-1 coefficients). The signature-side counterpart to crypto/mlkem_sample.rye, standing on the GREEN base ring and the GREEN SHAKE XOF."
say "crypto-mldsa-sample: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: rejection-sample a uniform coefficient below q, map a nibble to a small centered secret, and place exactly tau signs in a ball by Fisher-Yates. Where ML-KEM sampled two distributions, ML-DSA samples three, the challenge ball the shape the KEM never needed."
say "crypto-mldsa-sample: Lens TAME — bounded loops (every squeeze buffer names a ceiling and raises SampleExhausted rather than overrun), contract asserts on every function, canonical residues throughout, secret-sampler bounds depending only on the public eta or tau. Correctness proven by self-consistency: RejNTTPoly matches an independent 24-bit bit-reader over the same GREEN SHAKE stream, RejBoundedPoly carries the CoefFromHalfByte known-answers and the centered range, and SampleInBall produces exactly tau +/-1 coefficients (Hamming weight tau), all deterministic. Data-independent for its public use; constant-time timing-safety the named horizon. Purely local — no key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/mldsa_sample"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/mldsa_sample.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-mldsa-sample: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/mldsa_sample.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-mldsa-sample: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-mldsa-sample: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-mldsa-sample' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-mldsa-sample: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-mldsa-sample line"
